Procedure
1. Started the Minikube Kubernetes cluster using Docker as the driver.
2. Verified that the Kubernetes node was in the Ready state.
3. Pulled the Python Flask application Docker image from Docker Hub.
4. Created a Kubernetes Deployment YAML file named python-deployment.yaml.
5. Configured the deployment with two replicas and container port 5000.
6. Applied the deployment configuration to Kubernetes.
7. Verified the deployment and checked the status of both pods.
8. Waited for both Python application pods to reach the Running state.
9. Created a Service YAML file named python-service.yaml.
10. Configured the Service using NodePort to expose the application on port 5000.
11. Applied the Service configuration and verified the service details.
12. Retrieved the application URL using Minikube.
13. Opened the URL in a web browser and verified that the Python Flask Demo App was running successfully.
